set terms_and_conditions = $terms$Movers Nationwide Ltd • Terms and Conditions of Service
Last Updated: 12 November 2026
Company Name: Movers Nationwide Ltd (Registered in England and Wales under Company No. 13187418)
Registered Office: Suite 10 Northlight Parade, Nelson, Lancashire, England, BB9 5EG

1. Definitions and Interpretation
In these Terms and Conditions (“Terms”):
- “Company,” “we,” “us,” or “our” means Movers Nationwide Ltd (Company No. 13187418).
- “Customer,” “you,” or “your” means the individual or business entering into a contract with us for removal and relocation services.
- “Consumer” means an individual acting for purposes wholly or mainly outside their trade, business, craft, or profession, as defined under the Consumer Rights Act 2015.
- “Subcontractor” means any independent, vetted third-party removal company or local provider engaged by us to perform the physical removal, packing, loading, or transit services.
- “Goods” means all furniture, items, boxes, and effects to be removed, transported, or stored under this agreement.

2. Basis of Contract & Subcontracting
2.1 Formation of Contract: A binding contract between you and Movers Nationwide Ltd is formed when we issue a written Booking Confirmation and receive your required booking deposit.
2.2 Use of Subcontractors: We coordinate nationwide removals by engaging a network of independent, vetted Subcontractors. By accepting these Terms, you expressly authorise Movers Nationwide Ltd to subcontract the physical execution of your removal to a suitable Subcontractor.
2.3 Our Legal Responsibility to You: Where you contract with us as a Consumer, our use of a Subcontractor does not affect your statutory rights against us under the Consumer Rights Act 2015. We remain responsible to you for ensuring that the removal services are carried out with reasonable care and skill, and we will manage all communications, logistics, and claims directly with you.
2.4 Job Sheets & Consignment Notes: On the day of the move, the attending Subcontractor may ask you to sign a Job Sheet, Inventory List, or Consignment Note confirming collection, delivery, and the condition of Goods. Signing such operational paperwork does not create a separate contract or override these Terms.

3. Quotations, Estimates, and Pricing
3.1 Validity: Written quotations remain valid for 28 days from the date of issue. All prices quoted are in Pounds Sterling (£).
3.2 Accuracy of Information: Our quotation is based strictly on the inventory list, property access details, and postcodes provided by you at the time of booking.
3.3 Additional Charges: We reserve the right to amend the price or apply reasonable additional charges if the scope of work changes on the day due to factors not disclosed prior to booking, including:
- Additional Goods not listed on your agreed inventory.
- Restricted vehicle access requiring a smaller shuttle vehicle or a long carry exceeding 25 metres from the vehicle to the property entrance.
- Unforeseen flights of stairs, non-working lifts, or lack of pre-arranged parking/dispensations.
- Waiting time charges (charged at £50 per hour per crew member) if delays are caused by late key release or property access issues beyond our control (typically after a 1 hour grace period).

4. Payments and Liens
4.1 Deposit: A booking deposit of between 20% - 40% of the total quoted fee is payable upon booking to secure your removal date.
4.2 Final Balance: Unless otherwise agreed in writing, the remaining balance must be paid in cleared funds no later than 72 hours before the booking date via bank transfer or debit/credit card.
4.3 Right of Lien (Commercial & Late Payment): If you fail to pay any sums due under this contract, we (and our Subcontractors acting on our behalf) reserve the right to withhold or store the Goods until full payment—including any reasonable storage and administrative costs incurred—is received.

5. Statutory Cancellation Rights & Rescheduling
5.1 Statutory 14-Day Cooling-Off Period (Consumers Only): Under the Consumer Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013, where you book online or over the phone, you generally have a statutory right to cancel within 14 days of entering into the contract.
Exception for Dated Transport Services: Please note that under Regulation 28(1)(h), contracts for the transport of goods on a specific date or within a specific period are exempt from the statutory 14-day cooling-off right. Therefore, our standard cancellation terms in Clause 5.2 apply from the moment of booking.
5.2 Cancellations by You: If you cancel your booking, the following charges apply to reflect our administrative costs and the financial commitment made to our Subcontractor:
- More than 7 clear days before the removal date: Full refund of your deposit, less a £100 administrative fee.
- Between 7 days and 24 hours before the removal date: Forfeiture of your 100% booking.
5.3 Postponement / Rescheduling: You may reschedule your move once free of charge if you notify us in writing at least 7 days prior to the scheduled start time, subject to availability. Postponements requested with less than 72 hours’ notice will incur a £100 rescheduling fee.

6. Your Responsibilities
You agree to:
- Declare in writing prior to the move any fragile, high-value, or unusually heavy items (e.g., pianos, safes, antiques, fine art, or marble).
- Ensure all boxes are properly packed, taped, and suitable for transit, unless you have purchased our full packing service.
- Empty, defrost, and disconnect all domestic appliances (washing machines, dishwashers, fridges/freezers) prior to arrival. (Note: Neither we nor our Subcontractors are qualified to disconnect gas appliances or hardwired electricals; you must arrange a Gas Safe registered engineer or qualified electrician).
- Arrange and pay for any necessary local council parking permits, bay suspensions, or loading permissions at both collection and delivery addresses. You will be liable for any Penalty Charge Notices (PCNs) incurred where legal parking was not provided.
- Be present (or have an authorised adult aged 18+ present) throughout loading and unloading to check that nothing is left behind and to sign off on the move.

7. Excluded and Prohibited Items
Neither Movers Nationwide Ltd nor our Subcontractors will transport:
- Dangerous, hazardous, or illegal substances (including gas cylinders, petrol, aerosols, paints, solvents, fireworks, firearms, or ammunition).
- Perishable, refrigerated, or frozen food, or live plants/animals.
- Cash, bullion, jewellery, watches, precious stones, deeds, securities, stamp/coin collections, or irreplaceable personal documents. You must transport these items yourself.

8. Liability for Loss or Damage
8.1 Standard Liability (Limited): Where we or our Subcontractors fail to exercise reasonable care and skill resulting in loss of or physical damage to your Goods, our liability is limited to the reasonable cost of repair or replacement (taking into account age, wear, and depreciation), up to a maximum limit of £50 unless you have declared a higher value and purchased Enhanced Liability Protection prior to the move.
8.2 Statutory Carve-Out (UK Mandatory): Nothing in these Terms limits or excludes our liability for:
- Death or personal injury caused by our negligence or the negligence of our Subcontractors;
- Fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; or
- Any breach of your statutory rights under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 that cannot lawfully be excluded.
8.3 Exclusions from Liability: We shall not be liable for loss or damage arising from:
- Owner-Packed Boxes: Damage to contents of boxes packed by you (“Packed by Owner”), unless there is clear external damage to the box caused by mishandling.
- Flat-Pack Furniture: Structural damage or loosening of joints to dismantled or assembled flat-pack furniture (e.g., chipboard/MDF items), which is inherently unsuitable for transport once assembled.
- Electrical & Mechanical Derangement: Internal failure of televisions, computers, white goods, or electronic equipment where there is no evidence of external physical impact.
- Pre-Existing Wear: Normal wear and tear, gradual deterioration, or pre-existing defects.
8.4 Business Customers (B2B): If you are contracting with us in the course of a business, our total aggregate liability under or in connection with the contract shall not exceed 100% of the fees paid by you for the services, and we shall have no liability for any loss of profit, business interruption, or indirect/consequential loss.

9. Time Limits for Claims
9.1 Visible Damage: Any visible loss or damage to Goods or property must be noted on the Subcontractor’s Job Sheet/Delivery Note at the time of delivery wherever reasonably possible.
9.2 Notification Window: You must notify Movers Nationwide Ltd in writing (via email to contact@moversnationwide.co.uk) of any loss or damage within 7 days of delivery (or within 7 days of when the Goods should have been delivered in the case of total loss). Providing photographic evidence and proof of value will assist us in resolving your claim promptly with our Subcontractor’s Goods in Transit insurer.

10. Events Outside Our Control (Force Majeure)
We shall not be liable for any delay or failure to perform our obligations caused by events beyond our reasonable control, including severe weather, road closures, major traffic accidents, vehicle breakdown, strikes, or government restrictions. In such circumstances, we will notify you as soon as possible and work with you to rearrange the service at no extra charge.

11. Data Protection (UK GDPR)
We process your personal data in accordance with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018. By booking with us, you acknowledge that we will share relevant contact, address, and inventory details with our assigned Subcontractor solely for the purpose of fulfilling your removal. Full details are set out in our Privacy Policy at www.moversnationwide.co.uk

12. Complaints & Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR)
If you are dissatisfied with any aspect of our service, please contact our Customer Resolution Team at contact@moversnationwide.co.uk so we can investigate and seek to resolve the matter promptly. If we cannot resolve a Consumer dispute internally, you may refer the matter to an independent Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) provider.

13. Governing Law and Jurisdiction
These Terms and any dispute or claim arising out of or in connection with them (including non-contractual disputes or claims) shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales. The courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim (save that Consumers resident in Scotland or Northern Ireland may also bring proceedings in their local courts).$terms$;
